# Script to post-process the raw RDF-XML Output generated by LLM.
# Step 1: Every string that is invalid xml i.e. outside of transaction logic gets commented out, because it resembles additional comments from the LLM.
# Step 2: Inserts RDF header around the entire data, also adds 2 generic elements (<gams:isMemberofCollection> and <gams:isPartOf>)
# Step 3: Fixes invalid strings that are common bugs in the LLM output. Can be extended/adapted as needed.
# Step 4: Remove empty lines from the output.
# Step 5: Validates/sanitizes the RDF by splitting multinode properties into valid RDF (f.e. 1 bk:transfers with 2 children bk:Money gets converted to 2 bk:transfers with 1 child bk:Money for each)
# Step 6: Resolves date phrases deterministically. The LLM is asked to COPY the date phrase
#         out of the entry into bk:when/@resolve-from rather than to compute a date; this step
#         turns the phrase into an ISO date with latin_dates.py (next to this file). Where a
#         block carries no @resolve-from (older output, or an entry with no date phrase), the
#         step falls back to VERIFYING the existing bk:when and only reports what it would
#         have computed.
# Step 7: Validates the RDF against the JSON that was fed to the LLM: every id present (no missing/extra/duplicate), each <bk:entry> equals the JSON entry, each arec:hasRubric matches the JSON rubric (compared by #anchor). The pointer/arec:recordedBy check is kept but stays silent for the ground-truth data in this repository, which carries no "pointer" field. Reports only — does not abort.
# Step 8: Final well-formedness check. Re-reads the file FROM DISK after the interactive
#         corrections of step 7 have been written, so it judges the file as it now stands —
#         not the in-memory tree. Verifies that it still parses, that the RDF skeleton is
#         intact and that no postprocessing leftovers remain.

# PIPELINE ORDER — IMPORTANT:
#   LLM_Processor.py  ->  postprocess_RDF_output.py (this script)  ->  compare_RDF.py
#   Run this on the raw output of LLM_Processor.py (output/JSONtoRDF/raw/), then evaluate
#   the postprocessed result against the ground truth with compare_RDF.py.

